  "notes": "Synthetic feeders (8 illustrative Karachi zones; feeder 2 hospital and feeder 6 water pump protected). Receding horizon: 12 hourly frames from 12:00 on 2026-10-28 (the last test day of the classical ridge forecast; weather source open-meteo-snapshot, demand and shortfall series synthetic). Each step solves a 3-hour window and commits only its first hour. The first window hour uses the actual shortfall (known when the hour starts); the later hours use the forecast. Hours past 23:00 wrap onto the same forecast day because no next-day forecast exists. Quotas are ceil(MW / 5) clipped to 0..4. The ledger starts at zero at 12:00 (earlier cuts that day are not modelled). Solver requested: exact. Frames solved by the quantum command: 0; by exact after a quantum failure: 0; by exact directly: 12. Every plan was re-evaluated here and checked for validity; exact_cost is the brute-force optimum of the same window. warm_started is true only when the solver that produced the plan was given the previous window's plan shifted by one hour (the exact solver never is). audit_passed is the audit of the window plan, including the daily-hours rule applied to the replay ledger."
